 "about_text": "Diversions Fine Arts is a membership gallery in Manhattan Beach, California, founded by arts writer and curator Genie Davis. It exhibits a wide range of contemporary artists from the greater Los Angeles area and beyond, working across mixed media, oil, acrylic, sculpture, and photography. Each month three artists are curated into a solo-style rotation, while group shows bring together artists from all membership tiers. The gallery operates on a low, 10% commission structure and also publishes the online magazine DiversionsLA.com, covering Southern California exhibitions since 2016. Its roster spans emerging and established artists working in painting, collage, neon, sculpture, and photography, reflecting a broad, inclusive approach to contemporary Southern California art.",
